{"id":"aura-plugins-7j072","title":"pasture-release: auto-sync (or warn) registered cross-repo marketplace on bump","description":"When a plugin IS registered in the plugin registry (claude-plugin-registry.json) with a cross-repo marketplace, `pasture-release <bump>` should auto-sync that plugin's marketplace entry to the new version — OR at minimum WARN that --plugin was omitted and the registered marketplace will drift.

Discovered: `pasture-release patch` released pasture v0.0.2 (plugin.json + tag + push) but left the pasture entry in aura-plugins marketplace.json at 0.0.1, because the cross-repo sync (runner.go step 9) is opt-in via --plugin. `registry sync-versions` does NOT catch this (it only checks intra-plugin file drift, not cross-repo marketplace entries). The footgun: easy to forget --plugin → silent marketplace drift, fixed manually post-release.

Options: (a) auto-sync registered plugins' marketplaces by default (with a --no-marketplace-sync opt-out); (b) detect registration and WARN/prompt when --plugin omitted; (c) extend `registry sync-versions` to also reconcile cross-repo marketplace entries against each plugin's plugin.json. Pick per the team's preference for explicit-vs-automatic.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"dayvidpham@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-06-04T11:32:18Z","created_by":"David Huu Pham","updated_at":"2026-06-04T11:32:18Z"}

